    answer: "SPF, DKIM and DMARC are domain-level controls that help receiving mail systems judge whether a message is authorised and authentic. SPF identifies permitted sending services, DKIM adds a cryptographic signature and DMARC tells receivers how to evaluate messages that fail alignment checks. They support deliverability and reduce impersonation risk, but correct configuration and ongoing ownership still matter.",
