    answer: "When a website goes down, customers may see an error, time out or reach only part of the service. The cause could be DNS, certificates, hosting, deployment, application code, a database or a third party. The first job is to define the impact and stabilise the service, not guess publicly. Preparation determines how quickly the right people can diagnose and recover it.",
